  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "COMEDY\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 9, CC 17 to 32\n   1 Kind of joke\n   2 What the joke is about\n   3 Pause before the punchline\n   4 Escalation\n   5 Absurdity\n   6 Deadpan to broad\n   7 Cringe\n   8 Setup and payoff\n   9 Scenes from setup to payoff\n  10 Laughs per minute\n  11 Who carries the joke\n  12 Reaction to the joke\n  13 Running gag\n  14 Callback\n  15 Rule of three\n  16 Physical comedy\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 9, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Wordplay\n   2 Misdirection\n   3 Irony\n   4 Understatement\n   5 Fish out of water\n   6 Visual gag\n   7 Subversion\n   8 Comic edit\n   9 Comic sound\n  10 Comic flaw\n  11 Comic premise\n  12 The topper\n  13 Oddly specific\n  14 Talking to the camera\n  15 Exaggeration\n  16 Humiliation\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 9, CC 49 to 64\n   1 The lie that grows\n   2 Misunderstanding\n   3 Cutaway gag\n   4 suite: Comedy lens\n   5 suite: Where the laugh comes from\n   6 suite: Deadpan\n   7 suite: Slapstick\n   8 suite: Mockumentary\n   9 suite: Screwball\n  10 suite: Cringe comedy\n  11 suite: Absurdist\n  12 suite: Dark comedy\n  13 suite: Rom-com banter\n  14 suite: Snowball disaster\n  15 suite: Pull-back reveal\n  16 suite: Smash cut contradiction\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 9, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Background gags\n   2 suite: Farce\n   3 suite: The topper\n   4 suite: Punching up\n   5 suite: The aside\n   6 suite: Oddly specific world\n   7 suite: Blind to their flaw\n   8 suite: The cutaway that contradicts\n   9 suite: Bigger than life\n  10 suite: Slow-burn gags\n  11 suite: Stranger in a strange land\n  12 suite: Twisting the familiar\n  13 pair: When a joke's setup is planted, the payoff lands\n  14 pair: When the escalation rises, the absurdity rises\n  15 pair: When the pause before the punchline grows, laughs per minute drop but each lands harder\n  16 pair: After a big joke, cut to a reaction\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 9, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: Two of a pattern, then the break\n   2 pair: \"I'll never\", then they do\n   3 pair: After a cringe, a pointed silence\n   4 pair: As trouble escalates, the frame widens\n   5 pair: A running gag returns, bigger\n   6 pair: A joke line returns in a tender moment\n   7 pair: Something absurd, nobody reacts\n   8 pair: Misdirection pays off with a pull-back\n   9 pair: After tension, a laugh breaks it\n  10 pair: When a joke lands, a topper follows\n  11 pair: When a lie wobbles, a bigger lie covers it\n  12 pair: When the lie collapses, someone is humiliated\n  13 pair: When a misunderstanding deepens, the chaos grows\n  14 pair: When someone is humiliated in front of others, the cringe rises\n  15 pair: When a blind flaw grows, the character is set back\n  16 pair: When a character talks to us, the others react a beat late\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 9, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: An oddly specific detail comes back later\n   2 pair: When the physical comedy turns destructive, things shatter\n   3 pair: When the joke is built on a misunderstanding, the confusion keeps getting deeper\n   4 pair: When the joke aims at the powerful, the audience laughs harder\n   5 pair: When the comedy goes cartoon-big, the falls get bigger\n   6 pair: When the payoff comes long after its setup, the laugh is bigger\n   7 pair: When the joke rests on the straight one, they stay perfectly calm\n   8 pair: When someone lands a sharp comeback, the pecking order wobbles\n   9 pair: When a disaster is treated as no big deal, the laugh comes in the pause\n  10 pair: When someone is badly out of place, the awkward moments pile up\n  11 pair: When more sight gags fill the frame, the laughs come faster\n  12 pair: When the setup feels very familiar, the payoff gets turned upside down\n  13 pair: When the comic idea is crystal clear, the scene can push it further and further\n  14 pair: When the situation keeps escalating, everything gets exaggerated\n  15 pair: When things get exaggerated far enough, they tip into the absurd\n  16 pair: When a cutaway shows the opposite of what was just said, the laugh lands on the cut\nCV-CC 7: MIDI channel 10, CC 1 to 10\n   1 pairs: Joke machine\n   2 pairs: Long-game comedy\n   3 pairs: Comic reversals\n   4 pairs: The camera sells the joke\n   5 pairs: The farce engine\n   6 pairs: Stacking laughs\n   7 pairs: Comedy of a flaw\n   8 pairs: Smash and scatter\n   9 pairs: The cartoon spiral\n  10 pairs: The calm one cracks"
   },
